  "answer": "The file is 1602 lines and `shift` sits at the very end. Let me inspect it in a line window to confirm the context before editing.\nConfirmed: the file is mostly boilerplate handlers, and the bug is on the last line — `table[key + 1]` returns the next element instead of `table[key]`. Making the minimal edit to just that lookup expression:\nEdit applied. Now let me check the test setup and run the tests:\nNo script defined in package.json. Let me try running the test directly with Node:\nThe test failed — let me see the full failure details:\nThe test uses an extensionless import which bare Node ESM can't resolve. Let me check the test file's import and what runners are available:\nThe test uses `bun:test` — Bun is the intended runner and it's installed. Running the test:\nTest passes. Quick final verification of the changed line:\n## Summary\n\n**Bug fixed:** `shift(table, key)` in `src/registry.ts` was returning `table[key + 1]` — the element *after* the requested key — instead of the element at the key itself.\n\n**What I did:**\n1. Located the function via grep (it sits on line 1602, the last line of a 1602-line file that is otherwise boilerplate `handlerNNNN` exports), and confirmed context with a line-window read.\n2. Made a single minimal edit to the lookup expression only:\n   ```diff\n   -export function shift(table: number[], key: number) { return table[key + 1] }\n   +export function shift(table: number[], key: number) { return table[key] }\n   ```\n3. Ran the test with **Bun** (the intended runner, since `test/oracle.test.ts` imports from `bun:test`):\n   ```\n   (pass) lookup at the key\n   1 pass, 0 fail, 3 expect() calls\n   ```\n\n**Integrity:** The file still has 1602 lines and only that one line changed — all other exports (`handler0`–`handler1600`, etc.) are untouched. `AGENTS.md`, `package.json`, and the test file were not modified, and no configuration was added."
